            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case concerns whether Congress can require U.S. passports for people born in Jerusalem to list \u201cJerusalem, Israel\u201d as the place of birth, or whether that authority is exclusively held by the President."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner and Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "23b8a204b8836873f7e4a1f94a1661b5b4eca0831e9c1819020e8c1cf7943f55",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-23b8a204b883-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "23b8a204b8836873f7e4a1f94a1661b5b4eca0831e9c1819020e8c1cf7943f55",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-23b8a204b883-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Both sides argue that the issue raises separation\u2011of\u2011powers questions and whether the dispute is a justiciable political question."
      }
    ],
